    "testIdPattern": "[direct/page-content-and-media.cs] PdfAsyncShouldReturnPdfBytes",
    "platforms": ["darwin", "linux", "win32"],
    "parameters": ["webkit"],
    "expectations": ["SKIP"],
    "comment": "PDF generation is Headless-Chromium-only (CDP Page.printToPDF); WebKit has no equivalent, so WKPage.PdfAsync throws NotSupportedException. Permanent skip, not a gap."
  },
  {
    "testIdPattern": "[direct/page-console.cs] should work",
    "platforms": ["darwin"],
    "parameters": ["webkit"],
    "expectations": ["SKIP"],
    "comment": "macOS-14 WebKit 2251 uses per-frame Console sessions. Console.enable is not sent on the page target (upstream wkPage gates it behind !enableFrameSessions), so page.Console never fires until frame sessions are modeled."
  },
  {
    "testIdPattern": "[direct/page-event-pageerror.cs] should fire",
    "platforms": ["darwin"],
    "parameters": ["webkit"],
    "expectations": ["SKIP"],
    "comment": "Same macOS-14 WebKit 2251 frame-session gap: javascript errors arrive via Console.messageAdded (source=javascript), which is unavailable without per-frame Console.enable."
  }
